 "about": "The festivals the Vedic calendar marks (wiki: the Wikipedia page, English and, where there is one, Marathi, linked from the day card) (js/core/festivals.js applies the rules; docs/decisions.md, 2026-10-19). mr / en are the full names, short the label for a day in the month grid (each word fits a day on a 390px phone). A lunar rule names the amanta month (1 Chaitra … 12 Phalgun), the paksha, the tithi within it (1–15; krishna 15 is amavasya), the part of the day that decides it (kala) and which day to take when the tithi is in that part of the day on two days or on neither (tie). A solar rule names the sidereal sign the sun enters (rashi: 1 Mesha … 10 Makara … 12 Meena). A rule { before, days } is the `days` days before another festival (the Utsav, the nine days before Guru Purnima); {n} in its names is the day's number. adhika: festivals are kept in the nija month, never in an adhika month.",
